{"id":25994,"date":"2021-08-18T12:12:18","date_gmt":"2021-08-18T11:12:18","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/?p=25994"},"modified":"2023-05-17T10:55:09","modified_gmt":"2023-05-17T09:55:09","slug":"excel-macro-enabled-workbook","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/excel-macro-enabled-workbook\/","title":{"rendered":"Complete Guide To Excel Macro-Enabled Workbooks"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>For many business leaders, Excel is an important tool that helps them to integrate data into everyday business life.<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While most professionals understand how to input and view data in Excel, many don&#8217;t realise the ways in which this programme could benefit them.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One key feature that the team here at The Excel Experts love using is <a href=\"https:\/\/amzn.to\/3HA9kW8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Macros<\/a>. If you&#8217;re unsure about Macros and <strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">why you should be using an Excel Macro-Enabled Workbook in your business<\/span><\/strong>, then keep reading to find out more.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Is A Macro And Why Enable Macros On Your Workbook?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A Macro is an instruction that is written into your Excel Workbook and allows the programme to connect with other digital tools and<strong> conduct simple tasks automatically.<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once you have your macros ready and your Excel Workbook is Macro-Enabled, you can use them to automate simple tasks.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For example, if you want your Excel Workbook <a href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/how-to-lock-cells-in-excel\/\">to import data<\/a> from a certain platform at a set time each month, or to send a specific email at set times, then you can programme a macro to do this for you.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"563\" src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/Why-Enable-Macros-On-Your-Workbook.jpg\" alt=\"Why Enable Macros On Your Workbook\" class=\"wp-image-31979\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/Why-Enable-Macros-On-Your-Workbook.jpg 1000w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/Why-Enable-Macros-On-Your-Workbook-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/Why-Enable-Macros-On-Your-Workbook-768x432.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This approach will save you time and allow you to automate tedious tasks without the need for expensive software that you have to buy, learn and import your data onto.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">With a Macro-Enabled Workbook and a little help from Excel pros, like the team at<a href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/contact-us\/\"> The Excel Experts<\/a>, you can instruct Excel on exactly what you need it to do.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You&#8217;ll be able to use the Microsoft tool that you know and love to save you time and allow you to streamline your organisation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/enabling-macros-excel\/\">Enabling Macros In an Excel workbook<\/a>&nbsp;allows it to automate basic tasks and allows you to use and write new macros for your company.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"616\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/image-1-1024x616.png\" alt=\"image 1\" class=\"wp-image-31974 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/image-1-1024x616.png 1024w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/image-1-300x181.png 300w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/image-1-768x462.png 768w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/image-1-1536x924.png 1536w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/image-1.png 1680w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/616;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Creating a Macro and using it correctly can be tough, but making the workbook itself is easy enough. All you have to do is save the document, visit the drop-down menu where it says &#8216;Save As Type&#8217; and choose &#8216;Excel Macro-Enabled Workbook&#8217;.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The document will save as &#8216;*.xlsm&#8217;, which means that you can now <a href=\"https:\/\/amzn.to\/3HA9kW8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">enable macros<\/a> and write instructions that Excel will follow.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making and managing macros might sound very complicated, but with a little help from the team here at The Excel Experts, you can quickly and easily make macros work for you. We can also help with using&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/excel-vba-for-mac\/\">Excel VBA for Mac<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wide\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile\" style=\"grid-template-columns:22% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><a href=\"https:\/\/amzn.to\/40uatr0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"206\" height=\"264\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/101-Excel-Macros.png\" alt=\"101 Excel Macros\" class=\"wp-image-33090 size-full lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 206px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 206\/264;\" \/><\/a><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Learn 101 ready-to-use Excel macros and save yourself hours of work!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-black-color has-luminous-vivid-amber-background-color has-text-color has-background wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/amzn.to\/40uatr0\" style=\"border-radius:7px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Buy Now<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wide\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" style=\"text-transform:capitalize\">what is a macro enabled file type?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Excel macro-enabled workbook, also known as <a href=\"https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/office\/save-a-macro-24a026ef-3145-4bf8-a5f2-2fc7889ff74a\">Excel Macro-Enabled Workbook (.xlsm)<\/a> is a file extension used by Excel which allows you to save Excel documents with macros and Visual Basic for Applications (VBA) code.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/amzn.to\/3HA9kW8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Excel macros <\/a>are created using <strong>Visual Basic for Applications (VBA)<\/strong>, allowing users to automate tedious tasks in Excel such as creating charts, creating pivot tables and more.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They&#8217;re also incredibly useful for automating Excel tasks and can significantly save time and effort when working with large data sets o<a href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/guide-microsoft-excel-formulas\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">r Excel formulas<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"563\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/what-is-a-macro-enabled-file-type.jpg\" alt=\"what is a macro enabled file type\" class=\"wp-image-31982 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/what-is-a-macro-enabled-file-type.jpg 1000w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/what-is-a-macro-enabled-file-type-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/what-is-a-macro-enabled-file-type-768x432.jpg 768w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1000px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1000\/563;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" style=\"text-transform:capitalize\">what is a macro free workbook?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">An Excel macro-free workbook is an Excel file that has been saved<strong> without any macros or VBA code. <\/strong>These files are much smaller in size, making them easier to share and transport between Excel users.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because macro-free Excel files do not contain any code, they cannot be used to automate tasks in Excel, making them less flexible and efficient than Excel macro-enabled workbooks.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">However, Excel macro-free workbook files are ideal for users who do not need to use Excel&#8217;s <a href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/excel-automation\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">automation tools<\/a> or who do not want the security risks associated with <a href=\"https:\/\/amzn.to\/3HA9kW8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Excel macros.<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-cyan-bluish-gray-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-cyan-bluish-gray-background-color has-background is-style-wide\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><p><a href=\"https:\/\/click.linksynergy.com\/link?id=EJwqZBxBmNA&amp;offerid=1060092.1105404&amp;type=2&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.udemy.com%2Fcourse%2Fexcel-crash-course-full-tutorial%2F\"><img decoding=\"async\" border=\"0\" data-src=\"https:\/\/img-c.udemycdn.com\/course\/480x270\/1105404_aca0_22.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" class=\"lazyload\"><\/a><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" border=\"0\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/ad.linksynergy.com\/fs-bin\/show?id=EJwqZBxBmNA&amp;bids=1060092.1105404&amp;type=2&amp;subid=0\"><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"has-black-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Microsoft Excel Udemy Course &#8211; Excel from Beginner to Advanced 2023<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-vivid-green-cyan-background-color has-background wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/click.linksynergy.com\/link?id=EJwqZBxBmNA&amp;offerid=1060092.1105404&amp;type=2&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.udemy.com%2Fcourse%2Fexcel-crash-course-full-tutorial%2F\" style=\"border-radius:7px\" target=\"_bla